<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Higuera</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Higuera is a small village in the Vallegrande Province of the Santa Cruz <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">Department</a>, in the eastern Andean foothills of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/che-guevara">Che Guevara</a> was held in its schoolhouse after his capture by the Bolivian army in October 1967 and executed there on 9 October. It has since become a place of pilgrimage for admirers of Guevara.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/la-higuera.jpg" alt="La Higuera" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Its author is Augusto Starita. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Che_Guevara_statue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
